        why: "The first book of the Age of Madness trilogy — set a generation after Red Country, with characters who are children of the First Law world's survivors. If Red Country is the end of one era, A Little Hatred is the beginning of the next. The industrial revolution has arrived in the Union, the Northern balance of power has shifted, and Abercrombie has new types of violence to examine. Requires the full First Law reading order for maximum impact.",
